  "question": {
    "text": "A line <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> lies in the plane <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> such that it is perpendicular to the line <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The line <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> passes through the point of intersection of the given line and given plane. Which of the following points does not satisfy line <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>?</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Jw3JO",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
